<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Ollama on ByF (BaiFan) · Daily Deep Think</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/tags/ollama/</link><description>Recent content in Ollama on ByF (BaiFan) · Daily Deep Think</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>blog@baifan.site (ByF (BaiFan))</managingEditor><webMaster>blog@baifan.site (ByF (BaiFan))</webMaster><copyright>CC BY-NC 4.0</copyright><lastBuildDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:25:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.baifan.site/en/tags/ollama/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>PDF2Markdown: Layout Analysis and Structured Extraction for Large PDFs</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/pdf2markdown-intelligent-pdf-extraction-tool/</link><pubDate>Tue, 25 Nov 2025 14:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>blog@baifan.site (ByF (BaiFan))</author><guid>https://blog.baifan.site/en/pdf2markdown-intelligent-pdf-extraction-tool/</guid><description>&lt;h1 class="relative group"&gt;PDF2Markdown - An Intelligent Article Extraction Tool for Large PDF Documents&#10; &lt;div id="pdf2markdown---an-intelligent-article-extraction-tool-for-large-pdf-documents" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#pdf2markdown---an-intelligent-article-extraction-tool-for-large-pdf-documents" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://python.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#10; class="my-0 rounded-md"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; fetchpriority="low"&#10; alt="Python Version"&#10; src="https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.13&amp;#43;-blue.svg"&#10; &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#10; class="my-0 rounded-md"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; fetchpriority="low"&#10; alt="Code Style"&#10; src="https://img.shields.io/badge/code%20style-ruff-green.svg"&#10; &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://mypy.readthedocs.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#10; class="my-0 rounded-md"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; fetchpriority="low"&#10; alt="Type Checking"&#10; src="https://img.shields.io/badge/type%20checking-mypy-blue.svg"&#10; &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="LICENSE" &gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#10; class="my-0 rounded-md"&#10; loading="lazy"&#10; decoding="async"&#10; fetchpriority="low"&#10; alt="License"&#10; src="https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green.svg"&#10; &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Project Overview&#10; &lt;div id="project-overview" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#project-overview" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;PDF2Markdown is an intelligent content extraction tool built specifically for large scanned PDF files. It combines traditional OCR technology with modern AI large language models to intelligently extract pure article content from documents, automatically filtering out non-article elements such as images and tables. Mixed Chinese-English documents are fully supported.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Local RAG with Ollama and pgvector: Architecture and Retrieval</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/rag-system-complete-guide-langchain-ollama-pgvector/</link><pubDate>Wed, 27 Aug 2025 14:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>blog@baifan.site (ByF (BaiFan))</author><guid>https://blog.baifan.site/en/rag-system-complete-guide-langchain-ollama-pgvector/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Building a local Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system with Ollama, LangChain, and PostgreSQL pgvector enables offline document chunking, vector storage, and grounded generation. The sample code repository is available at &lt;a href="https://github.com/ByronFinn/rag-lab.git" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;rag-lab&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- more --&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Goals and Outcomes&#10; &lt;div id="goals-and-outcomes" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#goals-and-outcomes" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will get&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A locally runnable RAG system: embed your documents into a vector store, retrieve, and generate answers with an LLM.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;reusable&lt;/strong&gt; engineering scaffold: LangChain + Ollama + pgvector + uv.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview-ready&lt;/strong&gt; principles and code details: the full pipeline of retrieval, splitting, embedding, recall, reranking, and answer generation.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;System Architecture and Data Flow&#10; &lt;div id="system-architecture-and-data-flow" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#system-architecture-and-data-flow" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight-wrapper"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;7&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;8&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;9&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;┌────────────────┐ ┌────────────┐ ┌───────────────────────┐&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;│ Client/Frontend │ ──→ │ LangChain │ ──→ │ Ollama(Embedding/LLM) │&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;└────────────────┘ └────────────┘ └───────────────────────┘&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; │ │ │&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; │ ▼ ▼&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; └──────────→ PostgreSQL + pgvector &amp;lt;─────── Doc vectors&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; ▲&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; │&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; LangChain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ollama&lt;/strong&gt;: runs the LLM and embedding model locally (the examples use &lt;code&gt;qwen3:8b&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;qwen3-embedding:4b&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LangChain&lt;/strong&gt;: calls the Ollama API directly and orchestrates the flow of load → split → embed → store → retrieve → generate.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;pgvector&lt;/strong&gt;: PostgreSQL&amp;rsquo;s vector extension for storing and retrieving document vectors.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;uv&lt;/strong&gt;: a blazing-fast, reproducible Python dependency and virtual environment manager.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Prerequisites&#10; &lt;div id="prerequisites" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#prerequisites" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;OS: macOS / Linux / WSL2 / Windows (WSL2 recommended)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Installed: Docker (with Compose), curl&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Network access to the Ollama model repository (models are pulled automatically on first run)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Without Docker you can also install PostgreSQL + pgvector and Ollama manually — the steps are the same. This post assumes Docker launches the backend services in one shot.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>